TI  - Using mid-upper arm circumference to end treatment of severe acute malnutrition leads to higher weight gains in the most malnourished children.
PY  - 2013
AB  - Objective
The World Health Organization recommends discharging children admitted to nutrition programs treating severe acute malnutrition, with a low mid-upper arm circumference (MUAC 15%. When this recommendation is followed, the most severely malnourished children receive a shorter treatment compared to children that are less severely malnourished. This study assesses whether using MUAC >125 mm as discharge criteria eliminates this effect.
