AU  - Prasad, Vandana; Sinha, Dipa; Chatterjee, Priyanka; Gope, Rajkumar
TI  - Outcomes of Children with Severe Acute Malnutrition in a Tribal Day-care Setting.
PY  - 2017
AB  - To describe the nutritional outcomes of children with severe acute malnutrition (SAM) in a village-level intervention. This observational longitudinal study on 179 children aged <3 years was conducted in seven tribal blocks of Central and Eastern India with SAM managed in a comprehensive day care program. 76% children with SAM showed improvement over a 4-6 months period, with 37% shifting to normal anthrometric status. There was a significant shift in Z scores. This community-based intervention showed fair results for management of children with SAM at village level.
